Z||000000||Eric||03-20-2001||11:03 PM||||April 22 is the first "fun event" for the Central Ohio region SCCA solo 2 races.  This is the best one because there are fewer cars and other drivers will sometimes let you ride along if you ask nicely.  It's at the Dephi plant in Columbus tech starts at 8am and we start racing at about 10-10:30am through 4pm or so.  The cost is $25 for non SCCA members or $20 for members.  It's a great time, and they usually drive rain or shine.  You can bring your own snell rated helmet or one will be provided for you free off charge (I think I'll buy my own this year  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"> ).  Now Chadmad said he would come last year, but I didn't see him.  Can I expect to see you this year, Chadma?||||reg||1
Z||000001||firstfiero||03-21-2001||10:14 AM||||        This might be a dumb question but are their any safty issues with the cars. As in do you have to have the racing shoulder harness belts or anything if not I might try to be their. A friend at work drives to columbos for comic book conventions so I'll find out from him how far the trip is.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/rolleyes.gif">  I used to watch it every year at the york fairgrounds and always wanted to join in  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  .....then as soon as i get old enough to drive they stopped. Is their a web site so I can get a calender of events. Maybe they have some closer. ||||reg||5
Z||000002||ChadMan||03-21-2001||11:31 AM||||Why, that sounds like a challenge, Eric!  I'll see what I can do...<P>Do you think I would get more good out of the fun event (4/22) or the driver's school (5/6)?  I can't attend both...I am going to Ed's swap meet 4/27-29 and if I go to Fiero events three weekends in a row, I will be shopping for a divorce lawyer.<P>Also, is it true that 4-cyl Fieros are now competing in the H-stock class?||||reg||10
Z||000003||Eric||03-21-2001||12:52 PM||||I'd say the driver's school, if you have to choose.  I personally like the fun runs, because no one really cares too much about their times, so they let you ride along.  But at the driver's school, an expert autoxer will ride with you once or twice, and then drive your car to show you what it can really do.  It's a humbling experience; they're always faster.  <P>I don't know much about the class you will race in.  I think I'm in emod or c street preped if I keep my yap shut  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  I don't get out there to compete (mostly because I can't) I just like to drive.<P>There isn't any reason a poperly maintained street driven car should fail tech.  No special belts are needed, just a helmet.  If your really interested in doing this a lot, first fiero, I'm sure there's a regional chapter of the SCCA in your area if the drive is too far.  Last year there was a ratty 85 V6 and a nicely modded 87 GT with a custom front suspension at the fun event.  I was slower than both of them.<P>||||reg||1
Z||000004||firstfiero||03-21-2001||01:01 PM||||   Sounds great...what model fiero do you take their?||||reg||1
Z||000005||Eric||03-21-2001||11:55 PM||||I've got an 88GT with a 3.1 (hush, hush) and I think Chadman has an 88 coupe.  Don't worry about hurting your car either.  At an autox you'll hardly rev past 4000 rpm.  The cones can scratch up a new paintjob unless you have a bra, but if you're careful, you won't hit any.  Hell, there's beautiful vettes that show up every year and they don't look worse for wear because they swiped a few cones.||||reg||1
Z||000006||firstfiero||03-22-2001||10:51 AM||||       Not worried about that. Just want to get my car out their and drive it the way it should be driven!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/cool.gif">||||reg||14
Z||000007||Eric||03-22-2001||11:29 PM||||That's cool, Firstfiero.  We'll be sure to get ahold of you before the big event. <P>I've been doing bad things in parking lots just because I know the time is drawing ever nearer  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  I think autocrossing is one of the best things you can do to increase your driving ability on the road.  An afternoon of taking 90* corners at max speed will teach you more about your car than 10 years of driving. ||||reg||1
